Kent Paul Dolan <xanthian@well.com> wrote:
>In spork, it seems, some of the intrinsics /
>resistances "leak".

Reflection leaks personal-injury damage from some damage types, so
shock resistance and disintegration resistance still matter. (Cold
resistance already matters a little bit because of Asmo, and fire
resistance already matters a little bit because of the HP depletion
effect from fire traps.)

Elemental resistances leak against gaze attacks but not against breath
weapons or wands, so that magical eyes - a new late-game opponent - are
at least slightly *directly* threatening if you don't have a blindfold,
as well as having the nuisance value of being best fought blindfolded.

Magic resistance leaks against magic missile attacks so that Angels - an
endgame opponent - are actually worth paying attention to as something
other than a speedbump.

Magic resistance leaks against the touch-of-death spell because
otherwise there's pretty much no point having it. (Personally set
challenges such as "MR-less" are *irrelevant* to the general design of
the game.)

Magic resistance leaks against the destroy armour spell because
otherwise there's no point in high-level casters having it.

Now, having restored some challenge to existing content, and increased
class differentiation, and made weapon skills relevant for the entire
game (with the important feature of having no "Swing Dead Stuff" weapon
skill, so you always have the accuracy cap to contend with when wielding
a rubber chicken), and made a few arbitrary instadeaths a bit less
deathy (unresisted TOD spell and deadly poison do fat damage and reduce
your MaxHP, instead of killing you on the spot), there's room for
potential new content to be something other than a SLASH'EM-style arms
race or Yet More Fancy Speed Bumps.
